# Why this directory has no `user.rb`
#
# Wave 9 of seams split the conflated "who logs in / who pays / who
# has a profile" trio into three peer engines. The canonical demo
# addresses humans through `Auth::Identity` (engines/auth) and
# tenants through `Accounts::Account` (engines/accounts). Neither
# lives in this directory; both ship inside their engine.
#
# Hosts that need a domain User on top of `Auth::Identity` (extra
# columns: display name, avatar, locale, etc.) drop one in here and
# include the optional concerns:
#
#   class User < ApplicationRecord
#     belongs_to :identity, class_name: "Auth::Identity"
#     include Auth::Authenticatable        # credentials shim
#     include Notifications::Notifiable    # notify_email / notify_sms
#   end
#
# This demo doesn't need the extra columns, so it leaves the slot
# empty. See README.md and CHANGELOG.md for the rationale.
